the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the product type is *a text*.
    the is_complete of the awb admissibility check is *a truth value*.
    the missing fields of the awb admissibility check is *a text*.
    the awb article of the awb admissibility check is *a text*.
    the product type or null is *a text*.

the templates are:
    the awb admissibility check for *a text* is *a truth value* with *a second text* with *a third text* under table awb_admissibility_check.

the table awb_admissibility_check is, with first match:
    product type                     | is_complete | missing fields                                                                             | awb article
    "TreeFellingPermit"              | true        | "No missing fields."                                                                       | "Awb 4:5 - application complete"
    "Zorgtoeslag"                    | true        | "No missing fields."                                                                       | "Awb 4:5 - application complete"
    "BuildingPermit"                 | true        | "No missing fields."                                                                       | "Awb 4:5 - application complete"
    "SubsidieThuisbatterijFlevoland" | true        | "No missing fields."                                                                       | "Awb 4:5 - application complete"
    any                              | false       | "Unknown product type — this application cannot be processed under the current AWB shell." | "Awb 4:5 paragraph 1 - unknown product type"

the knowledge base awb_completeness_check includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/awb-completeness-check.dmn".

the product type or null is the product type, as stated in the model at decision Awb Admissibility Check.

rule awb_admissibility_check_2 with provenance the model at decision Awb Admissibility Check:
the product type or null is null if
    it is not the case that the product type is a text.

rule awb_admissibility_check_3 with provenance the model at decision Awb Admissibility Check:
the is_complete of the awb admissibility check is a truth value if
    the awb admissibility check for the product type or null is the truth value with a text with a second text under table awb_admissibility_check.

rule awb_admissibility_check_4 with provenance the model at decision Awb Admissibility Check:
the missing fields of the awb admissibility check is a text if
    the awb admissibility check for the product type or null is a truth value with the text with a second text under table awb_admissibility_check.

rule awb_admissibility_check_5 with provenance the model at decision Awb Admissibility Check:
the awb article of the awb admissibility check is a text if
    the awb admissibility check for the product type or null is a truth value with a second text with the text under table awb_admissibility_check.

